# Docker build context exclusions for the it-helpdesk agent image.
#
# This file has a second job beyond trimming the build context: the CDK
# DockerImageAsset appends every line here to its asset `exclude` list, so
# anything excluded below is also kept out of the asset fingerprint that
# becomes the AgentCore Runtime ContainerUri. That is what makes the
# synthesized template reproducible across machines — without it, a local
# .venv/ or __pycache__/ leaks into the hash.
#
# Do NOT exclude anything the Dockerfile copies: pyproject.toml, uv.lock,
# main.py, tools/, utils/.

# Local virtualenvs
.venv/
**/.venv/

# Python bytecode and interpreter caches
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
**/*.py[cod]

# Local toolchain pin — the image pins Python via its base image
.python-version

# Test, lint, and type-check caches
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# Packaging metadata
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/

# Local secrets. .env.example is documentation and stays in the context.
.env
**/.env
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
